  canonical_name ServiceSite
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/public-samples-browser.mjs
  witness packs/no-simulation/live-samples-20261013 records seven live pages at desktop and phone widths, 37 catalogue interactions, 26 planner interactions and a marked planner enquiry reconciled once into the native lead and held-message owners; exact test records were closed out without email
  family surface
  domain Surface / A service business's public site, built from one record
  layer presentation
  semantic_question What pages and sections does a service business's site have, in whose words, where do a visitor's requests go, and how does a second business get one without a second builder?
  purpose A kit of fifteen sections (hero, ask, door, proof, steps, compare, cases, person, reviews, listings, figures, calculator, amounts, library, call) around a shared shell. A page's one request form sits in its hero or in an ask section. A library section publishes a large collection as small compressed pieces (entries in runs, each kind's titles in pages, title words by first letters) that a phone fetches only on request, and says how much it has fetched. A site shows the contact routes it has; phone, name and email are each optional when the site keeps requests itself. A site is one record: the business, the contact, pages of ordered sections with their words, and a look. The look is stated in the same roles a presentation template carries, so a site can wear an authored estate language by name or state its own; every shade is worked out from those roles and an unreadable look is refused at build. The form is flat or stepped, with typed fields and stated choices. A site either hands requests to the visitor's mail app or keeps them with its own small server code, which accepts only the fields its own forms ask for; kept requests are brought into the CMS as service_lead rows. The record lives in the CMS as a service_site entry, is exported to the site folder, built to static pages with a stylesheet holding only what they use, and published to the Cloudflare account the record names.
  maturity implemented
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/document-recording.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/documents-recording.test.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/documents-recording-browser.test.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/documents-public-recording.witness.mjs
  invariant recording import retains the selected media and raw native transcript; adjacent unfinished sentences may join into a passage without changing their words or crossing a long pause, and every resulting time remains within the recording
  invariant recording search, playback and saved notes address the same source digest and paragraph; distinct paragraphs retain distinct revision-checked notes, including older notes saved under document-level keys
  invariant publisher source addresses permit only HTTP(S) without credentials; credit and source metadata participate in the recording identity
  invariant local recording playback uses a host-checked, session-authorized media endpoint with bounded byte ranges; its HttpOnly media cookie grants no source, search or removal API access
  invariant new document indexes use Nomic search_document inputs paired with search_query inputs, and record that profile in the index receipt; an older index keeps its original query encoding without restoring removed records
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/documents-recording.test.mjs exercises sentence spans, source identity, invalid times and paths, local media authority, removal and failed imports
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/documents-recording-browser.test.mjs exercises playback, highlighting, separate timed notes, reload, source removal and browser/server restart
  forbidden_inference playable media, timed retrieval or sentence grouping -> word-perfect speech recognition or automatic factual review
