  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/service-site.test.mjs builds two businesses from two records, serves each as it is published (files plus the site's own server code) and uses them in Chrome at 320, 390, 768, 1024 and 1280 wide: no failed load, script error or third-party script; on a phone nothing runs off the screen, every control is at least 44 px tall, no text is under 12 px, no field makes the phone zoom, and the menu opens and closes; a stepped form refuses to advance unfilled, the request it sends is kept with only what was typed, and when the server cannot keep it the mail app gets it and the page says so; the server code refuses another origin, another form, an unlisted field, an unstated choice, a missing phone, an oversized body, and keeps nothing from a filled trap field
  witness 2026-10-04 on the live site six requests from one address were answered 201 five times and then 429, and the browser fell back to the mail app; after the counter was cleared a marked request sent through the live buyers form on a phone was picked up by the scheduled job, became a service_lead row and a held outbound_message addressed to the business, and was then removed from the site and the CMS
  witness components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/service-site.test.mjs also searches, browses and reads a 1,000-entry collection on a phone-sized browser: nothing of it is fetched before a search, a 700-entry kind arrives a page at a time, an entry opens and deep-links, a title containing markup stays text, the whole visit takes under fourteen small pieces, and with no contact on record a request the server cannot keep is said to have failed
  witness 2026-10-05 the editorial look, drawn in Google Stitch from a brief written off the estate's own surfaces and applied by hand from its design system and screens (the editor took no automated pointer input, so its code was not exported), is live on https://aurekai-recipes.pages.dev/: serif roman and italic headline, paper and ink bands, numbered facts, hairline tables; no sideways scroll and no small tap target at 320 and 390 wide
  witness 2026-10-04 published from the live CMS record to a second Cloudflare account; every live page opened in Chrome at phone and desk width, one marked test request sent through the live form answered 201, was brought into the CMS by site.mjs leads exactly once across two runs, and was then removed from both
  invariant a section never names a colour and the shell never names a business; what differs between two sites is in their records
  invariant a look is a named way of drawing the same sections (the kit has two: editorial and night); it changes no word, no order and no behaviour, and a record cannot name a look the kit does not have
  invariant a review, a listing or a table of figures appears only when it is on file whole (a review with who said it, a listing with place and price, figures with source and day read); otherwise the section, its menu link, and a page left with nothing but its opening are absent
  invariant a record can ask for material only by a name the site folder provides; a record never runs anything
  invariant a library page holds none of its collection and fetches nothing of it until asked; titles and entries are placed as text, never as markup
  invariant an amounts section only switches between lists worked before the page was built; nothing is calculated in the browser
  invariant a request's own records can be consulted as it arrives through the site folder's lead hook, which reads and contacts nobody
  invariant the server code keeps a request only from this site's own origin, for a form this site has, with only that form's fields and stated choices, and records nothing about the visitor beyond what they typed
  invariant the page says a request was kept only after the server answered that it was; otherwise it says the mail app has it
  invariant a sender is counted under a one-way mark of its network address that lives an hour and is never stored with a request
  invariant bringing a request into the CMS writes a held message for the business and sends nothing
  invariant server-mode builds emit Pages invocation routes only for /api/lead and /api/lead/*; static pages, assets and data bypass the intake Worker
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/tests/routing.test.mjs
  witness 2026-10-08 routing.test.mjs first failed because the real build omitted _routes.json; routing, ordinary intake and catalogue review tests then passed 15 tests and 111 assertions. Rebuilding aurekai-work-samples preserved all 27 previous output files byte-for-byte and added only _routes.json
  witness 2026-10-08 site.mjs publish deployed the intake-only routing file to aurekai-work-samples on the estate account; Cloudflare production deployment 4abfc5fe-ca31-4798-b324-a5bcad9d74e4 reports success. Native observations before and after returned identical catalogue HTML SHA-256 a9033137e61bc58c955257bbf1c28bf648886f75e4e1226b95ad592d6cf1160d and HTTP 200; GET of the catalogue intake route returned its expected 405. No new browser walkthrough, stored submission, account usage reduction or Fleming deployment is claimed
  forbidden_inference restricted Pages invocation routes -> account-wide quota recovery, proof of the historical request-limit cause, or immunity of intake to other Workers exhausting the shared allowance
  invariant each lead sync reconciles saved unhandled requests with their stable outbound message identifiers before fetching remote requests; retries preserve existing messages and the saved fields and brief
  invariant a failed account fetch or individual request write is reported without preventing other sites from being processed; any reported error makes the command exit unsuccessfully
