  invariant catalogue intake and native review use the same retained product addresses, option identifiers and submitted field limits; a rejected identity receives no receipt and consumes no storage counter
  witness 2026-10-07 catalogue-review.test.mjs reproduces a 201 receipt for a substituted source address before the fix, then verifies refusal before storage for wrong addresses, unknown options and oversized SKU or tags; a real retained option passes generated intake and native review. Catalogue, review, lead recovery and ordinary intake regressions pass 29 tests with 169 assertions
  witness 2026-10-08 site.mjs publish deployed the shared catalogue identity checks to aurekai-work-samples on the estate account after one ENOSPC retry; native observation catalogue-intake-identity-20261008 returned HTTP 200 for the RED3 catalogue route. No fresh browser walkthrough or live submission was performed for this change
  invariant catalogue descriptions are projected once from retained HTML through pinned parse5; the browser uses that prepared text and both intake and native review compare submitted original values against build-derived SHA-256 field digests before retaining or enriching a review
  witness 2026-10-08 the invented-original regression first returned HTTP 201; the fix rejects forged title, description, tags, SKU and price originals before storage and in the native lead hook, while a five-field draft with a nonempty source description reaches the CMS review path. Catalogue, intake, routing and lead recovery checks pass 34 tests with 220 assertions
  witness 2026-10-08 site.mjs publish deployed the original-field checks to aurekai-work-samples on the estate account. catalogue-live-intake.test.mjs verified three published asset digests against the local build and HTTP 400 with no receipt for a marked invented original; one test and ten assertions passed. No fresh browser walkthrough was performed for this change
